| **Up to 200 accounts in one transaction** | A single batch job is enqueued; the platform splits it into ≤ 200 executions, each with its own 100-callout limit. No queued-job or callout limit is breached. |
| **`country` is null when blank** | `String.isBlank()` normalises `null` and `''` to `null`; `JSON.serialize` renders `"country":null`. |
| **18-char Id** | Trigger-context `Id` and SOQL `Id` are already 18 characters in Apex. |
| **Traceability for ERP** | Each request body is a single-element array containing exactly one `salesforceId`, so the ERP team can correlate 1-to-1. |
| **Error handling / retries** | Explicitly out of scope per the ticket; the response is sent and not further processed. |

