File: force-app/main/default/classes/LeadContactMatcher.cls
public with sharing class LeadContactMatcher {

    /**
     * For each lead, returns the Id of the first contact (in contacts order)
     * whose email matches the lead's email (ignoring case and surrounding
     * whitespace), or null. A blank/null email never matches.
     *
     * Uses a normalised-email → Id map so the method is O(leads + contacts)
     * rather than O(leads × contacts). At the stated maxima (3k × 3k) this
     * keeps CPU usage negligible inside the import transaction.
     *
     * This method performs no DML or SOQL.
     */
    public static List<Id> matchByEmail(List<Lead> leads, List<Contact> contacts) {
        // Build map of normalised email → first contact Id (preserving contacts order)
        Map<String, Id> firstContactByEmail = new Map<String, Id>();
        if (contacts != null) {
            for (Contact c : contacts) {
                if (String.isBlank(c.Email)) {
                    continue;
                }
                String key = c.Email.trim().toLowerCase();
                if (String.isBlank(key)) {
                    continue;
                }
                if (!firstContactByEmail.containsKey(key)) {
                    firstContactByEmail.put(key, c.Id);
                }
            }
        }

        // Resolve each lead
        List<Id> results = new List<Id>();
        if (leads != null) {
            for (Lead l : leads) {
                Id matchedId = null;
                if (!String.isBlank(l.Email)) {
                    String key = l.Email.trim().toLowerCase();
                    if (!String.isBlank(key)) {
                        matchedId = firstContactByEmail.get(key); // null if no match
                    }
                }
                results.add(matchedId);
            }
        }
        return results;
    }
}
```

**Key design points:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| Case / whitespace insensitive | `trim().toLowerCase()` as the map key |
| Blank email never matches | `String.isBlank()` guard before building the key (covers `null`, `""`, `"   "`) |
| First contact wins | `containsKey` check before `put` — iteration order of `contacts` is preserved |
| No DML / SOQL | Pure in-memory; no `insert`, `update`, or `SELECT` |
| Null-safe inputs | Null `leads` → empty list; null `contacts` → all nulls in the result |
| Result size/order | One entry per lead, same order, `null` where no match |

