```apex
public class PaymentPlanService {

    public class PaymentPlanException extends Exception {}

    public static List<npe01__OppPayment__c> scheduleInstallments(
        Id opportunityId,
        Integer numberOfPayments,
        Date firstPaymentDate
    ) {
        // Validate numberOfPayments
        if (numberOfPayments == null || numberOfPayments < 1) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException(
                'numberOfPayments must not be null and must be at least 1.'
            );
        }

        // Query the opportunity and verify it is open
        Opportunity opp = [
            SELECT Id, Amount, IsClosed
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE Id = :opportunityId
        ];

        if (opp.IsClosed) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException(
                'Cannot schedule installments on a closed opportunity.'
            );
        }

        // Query all existing payments for this opportunity
        List<npe01__OppPayment__c> allPayments = [
            SELECT Id, npe01__Amount__c, npe01__Status__c, npe01__Date__c
            FROM npe01__OppPayment__c
            WHERE npe01__Opportunity__c = :opportunityId
        ];

        // Partition into history (paid / written-off) and deletable (everything else)
        List<npe01__OppPayment__c> deletablePayments = new List<npe01__OppPayment__c>();
        Decimal historyTotal = 0;

        for (npe01__OppPayment__c p : allPayments) {
            if (p.npe01__Status__c == 'Paid' || p.npe01__Status__c == 'Written Off') {
                historyTotal += p.npe01__Amount__c;
            } else {
                deletablePayments.add(p);
            }
        }

        // Calculate outstanding amount
        Decimal outstanding = opp.Amount - historyTotal;

        if (outstanding <= 0) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException(
                'Outstanding amount must be greater than zero.'
            );
        }

        // Compute the base installment (floor to the cent)
        Decimal baseAmount = (outstanding / numberOfPayments).setScale(2, RoundingMode.DOWN);

        // --- DML: delete existing non-history payments ---
        if (!deletablePayments.isEmpty()) {
            delete deletablePayments;
        }

        // --- DML: build and insert the new installment payments ---
        List<npe01__OppPayment__c> newPayments = new List<npe01__OppPayment__c>();

        for (Integer i = 0; i < numberOfPayments; i++) {
            Decimal amt;
            if (i < numberOfPayments - 1) {
                amt = baseAmount;
            } else {
                // Last payment absorbs the rounding remainder
                amt = outstanding - (baseAmount * (numberOfPayments - 1));
            }

            newPayments.add(new npe01__OppPayment__c(
                npe01__Opportunity__c = opportunityId,
                npe01__Date__c = firstPaymentDate.addMonths(i),
                npe01__Status__c = 'Unpaid',
                npe01__Amount__c = amt
            ));
        }

        insert newPayments;

        return newPayments;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions:**

| Concern | Resolution |
|---|---|
| "Without changing anything" | All validation (param, closed opp, outstanding ≤ 0) happens *before* any DML, so no writes occur if the exception is thrown. |
| History preservation | Payments with status `Paid` or `Written Off` are excluded from the delete list and their amounts are subtracted from `Amount` to derive the outstanding. |
| Exact sum guarantee | Every payment except the last gets `baseAmount` (floored to 2 dp). The last payment is `outstanding − baseAmount × (n−1)`, which by construction makes the total exactly equal to `outstanding`. |
| Schedule order | Payments are built in a loop from `i = 0` to `n−1` and inserted in that order; the returned list preserves insertion order. |
| Bulk safety | The method operates on a single opportunity (as the API contract dictates), but all collections are list-based so it would work correctly in a governor-limit sense for the given input. |

