```apex
public class FamilyService {

    public static void linkParents(Map<Id, Id> parentIdByChildId) {
        if (parentIdByChildId == null || parentIdByChildId.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Collect all unique contact IDs involved (both parents and children)
        Set<Id> allContactIds = new Set<Id>();
        for (Map.Entry<Id, Id> e : parentIdByChildId.entrySet()) {
            if (e.getKey() != null) {
                allContactIds.add(e.getKey());
            }
            if (e.getValue() != null) {
                allContactIds.add(e.getValue());
            }
        }

        if (allContactIds.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // 1 SOQL: fetch every existing relationship that touches any of our contacts
        Map<Id, Set<Id>> forwardPairs = new Map<Id, Set<Id>>();
        for (OppRelationship r : [
            SELECT AccountOrContact, RelatedContact
            FROM OppRelationship
            WHERE AccountOrContact IN :allContactIds
               OR RelatedContact IN :allContactIds
        ]) {
            if (r.AccountOrContact != null && r.RelatedContact != null) {
                if (!forwardPairs.containsKey(r.AccountOrContact)) {
                    forwardPairs.put(r.AccountOrContact, new Set<Id>());
                }
                forwardPairs.get(r.AccountOrContact).add(r.RelatedContact);
            }
        }

        // Determine which pairs are new (no relationship in either direction)
        List<OppRelationship> toInsert = new List<OppRelationship>();

        for (Map.Entry<Id, Id> e : parentIdByChildId.entrySet()) {
            Id childId = e.getKey();
            Id parentId = e.getValue();

            if (childId == null || parentId == null) {
                continue;
            }

            Boolean alreadyExists =
                (forwardPairs.containsKey(parentId) && forwardPairs.get(parentId).contains(childId))
                ||
                (forwardPairs.containsKey(childId) && forwardPairs.get(childId).contains(parentId));

            if (!alreadyExists) {
                toInsert.add(new OppRelationship {
                    AccountOrContact = parentId,
                    RelatedContact = childId,
                    RelationshipName = 'Parent',
                    Status = 'Current'
                });
            }
        }

        // 1 DML: insert all new relationships in a single statement
        if (!toInsert.isEmpty()) {
            INSERT toInsert;
        }
    }
}
```

**How it works:**

| Concern | Resolution |
|---|---|
| **One record per direction** | We insert a single `OppRelationship` row (`AccountOrContact` = parent, `RelatedContact` = child, `RelationshipName` = *Parent*, `Status` = *Current*). NPSP's *List Setting* reciprocal method automatically creates the mirror row on the child, resolving the name to *Son*, *Daughter*, or *Child* via the configured gender-based lookup. |
| **Idempotent re-runs** | A single SOQL pulls every relationship touching any of the contacts in the batch. We index them as `forwardPairs` and skip any pair that already appears in either direction before inserting. |
| **Governor limits** | Regardless of batch size (200 pairs), the method executes exactly **1** `SELECT` and at most **1** `INSERT`, well within the 100-SOQL / 150-DML limits. |
| **Null / empty input** | Early-return guards on `null` / `isEmpty()` and per-entry null checks ensure no query or DML fires when there is nothing to do. |

